.TH MAIL-QUEUE 1 "2026-10-16" "SASD Freeware" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mail-queue \- bounded read-only Postfix mail queue summary
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mail-queue
.RI [ --timeout\ 1..30 ]
.RI [ --client\ ABSOLUTE_PATH ]
.RI [ --null ]
.br
.B mail-queue --input
.I FILE
.RI [ --null ]
.br
.B mail-queue --help | --version
.SH DESCRIPTION
Reads a local Postfix 3.1+ queue listing by executing only
.BR "postqueue -j" .
Aggregates queued messages, message bytes and remaining recipient counts by
queue. Does not disclose message bodies, queue IDs, sender/recipient addresses
or delivery failure reasons. Does not send, flush, retry, hold or delete mail.
A live listing is not atomic and may duplicate or miss messages as the queue
changes. The program does not provide Exim/Sendmail or old mailq text parsing.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --input FILE
Analyze a regular, readable, non-symlink JSON-Lines fixture offline.
Mutually exclusive with --client. Never starts postqueue.
.TP
.B --client ABSOLUTE_PATH
Use an explicitly trusted absolute regular executable, not a symlink.
Otherwise search for postqueue in absolute PATH components.
.TP
.B --timeout N
Whole native process timeout in seconds (1 to 30, default 10).
.TP
.B --null
Emit seven records of four NUL-terminated fields (queue name, message count,
byte count, recipient count) without a heading.
.TP
.B --help, --version
Display usage or version without contacting Postfix.
.SH OUTPUT
Tab-separated QUEUE, MESSAGES, BYTES, RECIPIENTS. Queues are maildrop,
incoming, active, deferred, hold, other, and TOTAL. Bytes are Postfix
message_size values, not on-disk consumption. Unknown queue names count
as other. Recipient counts are not unique email addresses.
.SH SECURITY
Uses only postqueue -j, with argv execution and no shell. Native stderr is
suppressed; only aggregate values are printed. Inherited MAIL_CONFIG and
MAIL_VERBOSE are cleared. Limits: 8 MiB total output, 64 KiB per record,
20,000 messages; malformed/truncated records produce no partial summary.
JSON::PP is required. Live Postfix integration has not yet been verified.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 complete listing without findings; 1 deferred/held/unknown queue entries
or native postqueue error; 2 invalid invocation; 3 missing prerequisite,
timeout, malformed/oversized data or incomplete listing. A native failure
returns no summary. A complete listing is not an atomic queue snapshot.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR postqueue (1),
.BR mailq (1),
.BR mail-probe (1)
